<Warning><message type="string">FOR TWO-DIMENSIONAL MODELS, IF A NON-UNITY THICKNESS IS SPECIFIED FOR TWO-DIMENSIONAL SOLID ELEMENTS AND THESE ELEMENTS ARE INVOLVED IN AN INTERACTION SUCH AS CONTACT, THE SAME THICKNESS SHOULD BE SPECIFIED FOR THE OUT-OF-PLANE THICKNESS OF THE CORRESPONDING SURFACE UNDER *SURFACE INTERACTION.</message><phase type="symconst">BATCHPRE_PHASE</phase><jobName type="string">Assemble_Tower</jobName></Warning>
<Warning><message type="string">NO HEAT FLOW WILL OCCUR BETWEEN SOME FACES OF THE SECONDARY AND MAIN PAIR (General_Contact_Faces, General_Contact_Faces). HEAT GENERATED AT THE INTERFACE WILL NOT FLOW INTO EITHER FACE. THE ROTATIONAL DEGREES OF FREEDOM OF THE NODES THAT CONSTITUTE THE SECONDARY SURFACE WILL NOT BE CONSTRAINED.</message><phase type="symconst">BATCHPRE_PHASE</phase><jobName type="string">Assemble_Tower</jobName></Warning>
<Warning><message type="string">The general contact domain for modeling contact interactions in Abaqus/Standard has double-sided facets. Initial contact adjustments for resolving gaps and  overclosures when a surface with double-sided facets is paired with any surface having double-sided facets may be incorrect. Similarly, adjustments for double-sided surfaces crossing each other may be incorrect and no additional warnings or error messages will be issued. In all these cases, we recommend using single-sided surfaces under *CONTACT INITIALIZATION ASSIGNMENT to  handle initial adjustments more precisely and avoid  possible convergence problems.</message><phase type="symconst">BATCHPRE_PHASE</phase><jobName type="string">Assemble_Tower</jobName></Warning>
